```

With `Version() == 2`, the first clause `calc.Version() != 1` is true, and because `Compatible()` returns `false`, `!calc.Compatible()` is also true, so the test fails. This is the compatibility-support stage of the staged migration: `Version()` must stay at `2` (as already required by `TestAVersion`, which asserts `Version() == 2`), and `Compatible()` must now report `true`.

